    "created_at": "2025-10-31T10:32:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-10-31T10:32:17Z",
    "body": "Gemini notes with some reformatting:\n\nAnne van Kesteren and Noam Rosenthal addressed logistics, including the cancellation of the next meeting due to TPAC and the use of the issue list for the agenda.\n\nKurt Catti-Schmidt, Olli Pettay, and Anne van Kesteren discussed the CSS Module proposal's stage advancement, the global scope for imports, and the preference for blob URIs over data URIs due to memory and observability concerns.\n\nStephanie Zhang and Anne van Kesteren covered the status of the form control range thread.\n\nAndreu Botella, Nicolò Ribaudo, Olli Pettay, and Anne van Kesteren provided updates on the Async Context TC39 proposal, suggesting the WHATWG stages process for web integration to address complexity, memory concerns, and engine implementability.\n\nEmilio Cobos Álvarez, Noam Rosenthal, and Anne van Kesteren debated the synchronous update of the `:focus-within` selector in an edge case, and Emilio Cobos Álvarez and Anne van Kesteren confirmed the closure of the `location.href` setter issue, aligning with current browser behavior and the specification despite its flaws.",
